@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{elfeed-extras.el} extends @samp{elfeed}@comma{} the Emacs RSS/Atom feed reader@comma{} with convenience commands for reading@comma{} filtering@comma{} and managing feed entries. The package depends on @samp{elfeed} and @samp{elfeed-show}.

The extensions address several common workflows:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Reading in EWW@.} Opening feed entries in the built-in EWW browser with automatic readability mode@comma{} providing a cleaner reading experience than many raw web pages (@ref{Reading entries, , Reading entries}).
@item
@strong{Entry management.} Marking all entries as read@comma{} copying entry URLs@comma{} and adding entries to a bibliography via @samp{zotra} (@ref{Entry management, , Entry management}).
@item
@strong{Filtering.} Toggling between showing all entries and only unread ones@comma{} or filtering by specific tags like ``wiki'' (@ref{Filtering, , Filtering}).
@item
@strong{Background updates.} Updating feeds even when Elfeed buffers are not open (@ref{Background update, , Background update}).
@item
@strong{Follow mode.} Automatically displaying entries as you move through the search buffer@comma{} similar to @code{org-agenda-follow-mode} (@ref{Follow mode, , Follow mode}).
@end itemize

