@node Reading entries
@section Reading entries

@findex elfeed-extras-show-visit-in-eww
Some feed entries are best read directly on the original website rather than in Elfeed's show buffer@comma{} but external browsers take you out of Emacs. The command @code{elfeed-extras-show-visit-in-eww} opens the current entry's link in EWW and automatically enables @code{eww-readable} mode once the page finishes loading. This strips away navigation@comma{} ads@comma{} and other clutter.

The command works in both @code{elfeed-show-mode} (using the displayed entry) and @code{elfeed-search-mode} (using the selected entry). Note that readability mode depends on the website's HTML structure and may not produce good results on all sites. This function is borrowed from Protesilaos Stavrou.

@findex elfeed-extras-jump-to-next-link
When reading a long entry with multiple hyperlinks@comma{} @code{elfeed-extras-jump-to-next-link} moves point to the next link in the entry and recenters the view. This makes it easy to scan through links without scrolling manually.

@node Entry management
@section Entry management

@findex elfeed-extras-mark-all-as-read
When you want to start fresh@comma{} @code{elfeed-extras-mark-all-as-read} selects all entries in the search buffer and removes the @samp{unread} tag from all of them. This is a bulk operation that affects every currently displayed entry.

@findex elfeed-extras-kill-link-url-of-entry
The command @code{elfeed-extras-kill-link-url-of-entry} copies the URL of the entry displayed in the show buffer to the kill ring. A confirmation message is printed in the echo area. This is useful when you want to share or save a link without opening it externally.

@findex elfeed-extras-add-entry
If you use a Bib@TeX{} workflow@comma{} @code{elfeed-extras-add-entry} passes the current entry's URL to @code{zotra-extras-add-entry} (from @samp{zotra-extras.el})@comma{} which handles adding it to your bibliography and downloading associated files. This command is only active in @code{elfeed-show-mode}.

@node Filtering
@section Filtering

@findex elfeed-extras-toggle-read-entries
By default@comma{} Elfeed shows only unread entries. The command @code{elfeed-extras-toggle-read-entries} toggles between showing all entries (including read ones) and showing only unread entries. It maintains its state in the variable @code{elfeed-extras-toggle-read-entries} (@ref{Filter toggle state, , Filter toggle state}).

@findex elfeed-extras-toggle-wiki-entries
For feeds that include wiki-tagged entries@comma{} @code{elfeed-extras-toggle-wiki-entries} switches between showing only unread wiki entries (@samp{+unread +wiki}) and showing all unread entries except wiki entries (@samp{+unread -wiki}). This is useful when you want to focus on a specific category of content. The state is tracked in the variable @code{elfeed-extras-toggle-wiki-entries} (@ref{Filter toggle state, , Filter toggle state}).

@node Follow mode
@chapter Follow mode

@findex elfeed-extras-follow-next
@findex elfeed-extras-follow-previous
Inspired by @code{org-agenda-follow-mode}@comma{} this feature automatically displays entries as you move through the Elfeed search buffer. Rather than selecting an entry to read it@comma{} you simply move the cursor and the entry appears in the other window.

The command @code{elfeed-extras-follow-next} moves the cursor down one line and displays the corresponding entry. The command @code{elfeed-extras-follow-previous} does the same upward. After displaying the entry@comma{} focus returns to the search buffer so you can continue browsing.

These commands use the internal helper @code{elfeed-extras-follow-entry} for the core logic and @code{elfeed-extras-display-buffer} for displaying the entry buffer without stealing focus.

