@node Background update
@section Background update

@findex elfeed-extras-update
The standard @code{elfeed-update} command requires Elfeed to be open. The function @code{elfeed-extras-update} first processes @code{elfeed-org} feed definitions (if @samp{elfeed-org} is available)@comma{} then ensures the database is loaded with @code{elfeed-db-ensure}@comma{} and finally triggers the update. This allows it to run from timers@comma{} hooks@comma{} or scripts without requiring an open Elfeed buffer. A message confirms that the update has started.

@node Filtering and display helpers
@section Filtering and display helpers

@findex elfeed-extras-filter-tags
@findex elfeed-extras-display-buffer
@findex elfeed-extras-follow-entry
@findex elfeed-extras-disable-undo
The function @code{elfeed-extras-filter-tags} applies a filter string to the search buffer via @code{elfeed-search-set-filter} and displays a message indicating the active filter.

The function @code{elfeed-extras-display-buffer} shows a buffer in the other window without selecting it@comma{} using @code{pop-to-buffer}. It is used internally by the follow mode commands (@ref{Follow mode, , Follow mode}).

The function @code{elfeed-extras-follow-entry} implements the core follow mode logic: it moves by LINES@comma{} recenters@comma{} displays the entry@comma{} and returns focus to the search buffer.

The function @code{elfeed-extras-disable-undo} sets @code{buffer-undo-list} to @code{nil} in the Elfeed search buffer@comma{} disabling undo tracking to save memory. It is intended for use in @code{elfeed-search-mode-hook}.

